description:
## Question

NoteEditor currently takes 20+ flat props. After the sub-primitive extraction, refactor to accept Svelte 5 snippets as named slot overrides — letting consumers replace individual form sections without understanding the whole API.

## Design

```svelte
<!-- NoteEditor.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  interface Props {
    sel: AnnotationRecord;
    onClose: () => void;
    children: Snippet;
    commentForm?: Snippet<[{ onChange: (c: string, t: string) => void }]>;
    tagsInput?: Snippet<[{ onChange: (c: string, t: string) => void }]>;
    readingSelect?: Snippet<[{ readings: Reading[]; onChange: (r: string | null) => void }]>;
    emphasis?: Snippet<[{ emphasis: Emphasis; onChange: (e: Emphasis) => void }]>;
  }
</script>
```

Default snippets render the extracted sub-primitives. Callers pass snippet overrides only for sections they customize.

## Dependencies

Requires: callback conventions ticket (onX props) + extract sub-primitives ticket (components to wrap in snippets).

## Contract

- NoteEditor accepts snippet props for each form section
- Default snippets render the extracted components unchanged
- No caller changes required for default behavior
- Gate: svelte-check 0/0, studio typecheck, studio vitest, browser smoke (open note, edit fields, close)

## Context

